Z||000000||Tryxalon||04-22-2001||11:41 AM||||I've heard several recommendations over the years, but what motor oil do <B>you</B> suggest for a 101,000 mile 2.5L Duke used primarily in town with temperatures from 20 to 70F ?? <P>WHY??? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||04-22-2001||11:55 AM||||On my duke with 100K miles I use (I forgot the company, its in a clear bottle with green cap) High Performance Synthetic Blend 20W-50  It is EXTREAMLY thick but i seem to get great oil pressure.<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||04-22-2001||07:32 PM||||I use Castrol 5w-30 in the winter and 10w-40 in the summer in my 84 duke with 203,000 miles.  Dosen't use any oil between changes. I'm afraid to go syn. because of the mils and the fact that the car dosen't leak.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tryxalon||04-23-2001||06:13 AM||||Being (currently) without either Owner's Manual or Shop manual (will have both) I'm just curious about what other people are using. <P>Been leaning towards 10w40 myself, but probably not synthetic because of the number of miles. <P>Other suggestions?? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spektyr||04-23-2001||02:02 PM||||How about suggestions for a 108k 2.8?<P>I was thinking of running high-grade 10w40 synthetic through it with a Bosch oil filter for about 1-2k miles to try to clean the motor out a bit.<P>Also planning to run the car for 15 min with a quart of diesel fuel in the oil to help dissolve any deposits in the oil runs.  The car was decently maintained, but by someone that doesn't really understand motors.  I figure it'd be good to 'flush' the oil as much as possible.<P>My reasoning/method make sense at all?<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jncomutt||04-23-2001||02:58 PM||||Hey, I came across this topic and found myself interested as well.  I don't know much about the different types of oils, (such as what the #s mean: ex.  10w40 vs. 5w30) nor much about synthetic except that its not too good to switch in a car with high miles.  <P>I too have an 84 I just purchased.  It only has 50387 miles and the oil has been kept up.  (The sticker on the window says 53k).<P>Is there an advantage to switching to synthetic and would I be able to?||||reg||1
